SUMMARY:New Moon Circle for All with Marian Noble
DESCRIPTION:Awakening Asheville\nJoin us for a welcoming and inclusive New
  Moon Circle\, where all bodies and all genders are invited into sacred ga
 thering. The New Moon is the seed point of the lunar cycle\, a powerful ti
 me to pause\, reflect\, and plant clear intentions for the month ahead.\n\
 nOur 90-minute circle opens with a grounding meditation to help you arrive
  fully in body and breath. We'll explore the astrological themes of this N
 ew Moon in an accessible way\, then move into heart shares\, holding space
  for one another in a supportive\, non-judgmental circle. We'll close with
  a ritual aligned with this month's lunar energy to anchor your intentions
 .\n\nYou'll leave with greater clarity\, deeper connection\, and inspired 
 momentum for the new lunar cycle. Whether you're new to moon rituals or a 
 longtime practitioner\, this circle offers insight\, community\, and renew
 al.\n\nWe gather on the eve of the Scorpio New Moon\, in the dark threshol
 d before the new cycle begins\, a powerful time to release what's complete
  and plant seeds of deep transformation.\n\nCome as you are. Everyone is w
 elcome. Bring your friends!\n\n**Details**\n\n* Sanctuary Studio\, 81 Weav
 erville Rd.\, Suite 2\, Woodfin\, NC 28806\n* Sunday\, November 8 at 7 - 8
 :30 p.m.\n* $22 per person. Space is intentionally limited to keep our cir
 cle intimate\, so reserve your spot early.\n* Please arrive a few minutes 
 early to settle in.\n\n**What to Bring**\n\n* A journal and pen\n* Any com
 fort items for your spot: blanket\, pillow\, bolster\n* An altar item\, su
 ch as a photo\, a crystal\, or something from nature\, to help hold the im
 print of our time together\n* Your sober self. This is a substance-free ga
 thering\, so come as your own sacred being.\n* Curiosity and an open mind 
 and heart\n\n**Our Circle Agreements**\n\n* **All are welcome.** There is 
 no competition or hierarchy here. No one is above or below another. We mee
 t as equals\, honoring the wisdom within each of us.\n* **Self-awareness o
 ver judgment.** If judgment arises (because we are human)\, see it as an i
 nvitation to self-reflect. We are all mirrors for one another.\n* **Confid
 entiality and respect.** This is a safe and sacred space. What is shared h
 ere stays here.\n* **Honor your needs.** Move as you need to: get water\, 
 use the restroom\, grab a tissue. You are a sovereign being and can care f
 or yourself.\n* **Emotions are sacred.** There's no need to hold back\, ap
 ologize\, or adjust your emotions to fit others. Your experience is your o
 wn medicine.\n* **Witness\, don't fix.** We honor each other as whole bein
 gs\, holding space without assuming needs or rushing to console. Simply wi
 tnessing is enough.\n* **Names and pronouns are honored.** Share yours if 
 you wish. We commit to using them as an expression of care\, presence\, an
 d mutual respect.
